dialect protocol
protocol stdio.semio.image.diff
version 1
schema s.stdio.semio.image
start body
framing record

# ARTIFACT-SYSTEM-OVERHAUL-REAL-CODECS-RUNTIME-REUSE-EVOLUTION image wave: REAL binary diff frame,
# replacing the old `print_diff().into_bytes()` text-as-binary shortcut (`🔺️diff/🦀️component.rs`'s
# old `DiffCodec::encode_diff`). `format u8` + `presence u8` (bit0=`width` bit1=`height`
# bit2=`colorspace` bit3=`bitDepth` bit4=`icc` bit5=`frames` bit6=`metadata`) are two REAL fixed
# fields; past that, 0-7 varint-length-prefixed opaque blobs follow (one per present field) —
# modeled as one opaque trailing `payload` chain rather than per-segment `Cond`-guarded fields
# because a SECOND `if`-guard on a field that was itself only conditionally decoded hard-errors
# `eval_cond` (`protocol-cond-cannot-chain`, same gap `✳️flow`'s/`✳️mesh`'s own diff protocols
# document). The real Rust `encode_diff`/`decode_diff` stays genuinely, fully structured
# (`write_str_lp`/`read_str_lp`, `store::pack_rt`'s real varint codec) — round-trip tested
# independently.
header fixed 2
field format u8
field presence u8

chain payload bytes
